  <h1>Editorial Standards and Publisher</h1>
  <p>classactionsettlementcalc.com is published by The Click Lab Agency LLC, a California limited liability company based in San Diego. The Click Lab publishes a family of plain-English legal and financial calculators; this site covers class action settlements from the class member&rsquo;s side.</p>

  <h2>Who publishes this site</h2>
  <p>Pages are drafted by the publisher&rsquo;s staff, checked against the primary sources listed on the <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a> (Rule 23, the Class Action Fairness Act, and the studies and decisions named there), and dated with the month of the last review. We do not use invented author names or credentials, and no one who works on this site is an attorney. If you want a named professional to rely on, that is a reason to consult one &mdash; the homepage explains where to get help.</p>
  <p>Corrections, questions about how a page was produced, and requests to see the sources behind a specific claim can be sent to <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a>.</p>

  <h2>Editorial Standards</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Primary source grounding:</strong> Factual claims about class action procedure are sourced to the Federal Rules of Civil Procedure, leading circuit court decisions on certification and settlement approval, and published settlement administration data — not to secondary summaries.</li>
    <li><strong>Documented methodology:</strong> Calculator allocation multipliers, claims rate baselines, and fee assumptions are documented in full on the <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>No sponsored content:</strong> The site earns money from display advertising and from the optional referral form described here; no sponsored articles or paid placements affect what we write. Separately, the homepage offers an optional, disclosed case-review form connecting readers with attorneys; see our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for what's shared if you use it. That referral product does not influence editorial content.</li>
    <li><strong>Currency:</strong> Pages are reviewed and updated when significant class action doctrine changes — new circuit decisions on cy pres, CAFA coupon settlement standards, or Rule 23 amendment guidance.</li>
    <li><strong>Scope clarity:</strong> This site provides informational content only — not legal advice or case-specific predictions.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Corrections Policy</h2>
  <p>If you identify a factual error — an incorrect procedural rule citation, a claims rate that is inconsistent with published administration data, or a settlement calculation that does not follow the documented methodology — email <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a>. Include the specific claim and your source. Corrections are reviewed within five business days.</p>

  <p>Return to the <a href="/">calculator</a> or see the <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a>.</p>
</BaseLayout>
